Merative is retiring the admission logic that ran inside the Advantage Suite data warehouse (the "Admission Build" batch process, documented in Chapter 9 of the Advantage Suite 5.4 Data Manager's Guide, IBM 2019) and replacing it with the Truven Flexible Analytics Inpatient Admission Grouper, an API-driven methodology that reads a medical claims file and returns admission-level output files (Methodology Guide v11.12.0, general availability December 2025). Both build the same thing: one record per inpatient stay, assembled from facility room-and-board claims and the facility and professional claims that fall inside the stay, with length of stay, financial totals, DRG, disease stage and outlier flags attached.
Our reporting depends on those admission-level values. This note is for the data team: it lists only the calculations that differ between the two guides, what each side does, and what that means for the numbers we publish and the joins we maintain. The full section-by-section walkthrough, field matrix and validation plan are in the companion file Merative_Admissions_Methodology_Parity_Comparison_Detailed.docx.
Documents compared
	Legacy	New
