What matters most
Five changes will visibly move reported numbers or break existing logic: length of stay is now a calendar difference rather than a sum of covered days; admission IDs are rebuilt on every run with no lineage to the old adm_id; the readmission-gap fields use blank instead of 0 and have no 365-day cap; the output field named "drg" is a pass-through of the claim DRG, not the grouper result; and the legacy rule that deleted zero-dollar (voided) admissions is no longer documented. Everything else in the table is a smaller shift or a documentation gap to confirm with Merative.
How to read the table
Only calculations that differ are listed, ordered by impact. Everything not listed here reconciled as equivalent (admit/discharge dates, transfer detection, financial summation rules, cost-trim thresholds, MDC/DRG-final mapping, disease category and stage, primary-physician selection). Cross-checked against the internal "Merative v11 Admission Methodology Review" (which cites the new guide as v11.2.0; the cover reads 11.12.0). Items marked Unclear are documented in the legacy guide but not addressed in the new one; confirm with Merative or in output data before relying on them.
